>> title: Hash Browns
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: potatoes, breakfast, griddle, crisp, stovetop
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: hashbrowns, hash brown potatoes, shredded hash browns, shredded potatoes
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: shred into cold water, soak 5 min
>> step.2: squeeze bone dry in a towel
>> step.3: press into the fat, fry 6 min, flip, fry 4 min
>> step.4: salt the moment they come out

Shred @russet potatoes{1 1/2%lb}(700 g; peeled) on the coarse side of a #box grater{} straight into @cold water{2%qt}(1.9 L) and ~soak{5%min}, changing the water once, until it stops going cloudy.

Squeeze @&(~1)shredded potato{} bone dry in a #clean tea towel{}, a fistful at a time. This is the dish: water left in the shreds steams the pile from the inside, and steamed potato is grey and limp however long it sits on the heat.

Press @&(~1)dry shreds{} into @clarified butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) in a #skillet{} over medium heat in an even cake and fry undisturbed ~fry{6%min}, then flip it in one piece and fry ~fry{4%min}.

Salt @&(~1)hash browns{} the moment they leave the pan with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp}(4 g) and @black pepper{1/4%tsp}.
